{
 "id": "media/big-image-small-conversation/bill-below-media-price/5m",
 "description": "One request: an image of 2,000,000 bytes, which the library prices at 8,000 tokens. The provider billed the whole request 2,350 tokens (text 750 + image about 1,600), so the bill is below the library price. The library cuts the media to the bill less the least the text can cost. Forwarded text: 2,000 + 1,000 = 3,000 bytes. The least is 0.05 x 3,000 = 150 tokens. The media gets 2,350 - 150 = 2,200 tokens. The text ratio is 150 / 3,000 = 0.05. The operator cuts m2 from 8,000 to 1,000 bytes: 7,000 x 0.05 = 350 tokens saved. This is the lowest figure the bill allows, so it is a floor. The check media_tokens fails to say the media price was cut. The request is not dropped: before the fix nothing was priced (unpriced ratio_range, saved 0). The baseline bill is 10,000 x 0.05 + 2,200 = 2,700 tokens: 2,700 - 2,350 = 350.",
